==County coding==
Georgia used two sets of numeric county codes on its license plates between 1957 and 1970. On both sets, the order of the codes was based on the respective populations of each county, with the order of the codes from 1962 onwards based on the figures according to the [[1960 United States census]].<ref>{{cite web|title=Georgia license plate County Codes |url=https://www.georgiaplates.com/county-codes |publisher=GeorgiaPlates.com |access-date=21 March 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|last=Nicholson |first=David |date=11 February 1999 |title=Georgia County Codes |url=http://www.15q.net/gaco.html |publisher=15q.net |access-date=24 December 2014}}</ref>

Since 1971, the name of the county of issuance has been displayed at the bottom of each plate – originally on a sticker, before becoming screened in 2012.

